# Client source material. Print artwork, layered files and review decks, around
# 90MB of it. The web-ready cuts live in assets/img/ and are committed; these
# originals stay out of the repo. A plain `git add -A` sweeps them in otherwise.
#
# Deliberately not a blanket *.pdf rule: product datasheets are the kind of thing
# this site will want to serve, and those belong in the repo.
Prince Label/
*.ai
*.psd
px98 website amendment*.pdf
Part 1 PX98 Website Amendments*.pdf

# The client's photography drop: 2560px PNGs, 52MB of them. The 2000px JPEGs cut
# from these live in assets/img/ and are committed; the originals stay out.
Sample Images/

# The client's drops, around 400MB between them: 4725px pack renders and 8K
# photography under client_image/, the approved photography set under Selected/, and
# the 26 Aug amendment deck and its four bottles under client_latest_amendament/.
# tools/build-images.py turns all three into what assets/img/ actually serves, and
# only those cuts are committed.
client_image/
Selected/
client_latest_amendament/
